msm: blocks are sized and placed with the PC header, on MPT_PC
Applied in order by runtimes/gc_wii/mp4/CMakeLists.txt with `git apply`.

ADR 0008, "Gate status after the implementation", finding 1. msmMemAlloc sized and placed every block
for the console's 32-byte MSMBLOCK, but on a 64-bit host the header is 48 bytes (three pointers). A
block's user area therefore started 16 bytes later than msm accounted for, each block used 16 bytes
more than it reserved, and a heap filled close to its end ran past it into the next HuMem block.
On PC, MSMBLOCK is padded to 64 bytes so the user area keeps the console's 32-byte alignment, a
static assertion pins that size on every 64-bit host (LLP64 and LP64), and msmMemAlloc sizes,
places and zeroes blocks with sizeof(MSMBLOCK). msmMemFree already found the header with base[-1].
A request larger than the heap, or a block whose end would pass the heap's end, returns NULL.
Changes how msm lays out its heap, so state hashes move (docs/titles/mp4.md section 11).

